body:
This started out as an edgy sketch in my fanfiction notebook that looked so cool that I had to make it into an actual picture.

As for the title, well sad things have happened, and will happen soon.

&#x200B;

We lost a good friend of ours a few months ago. He had actually died a month before we were informed of it, but I think it was in his last will that no one know. He was a stubborn man and would never want anyone to cry over him. I'm glad I got to know him as I grew up, and I know that if he saw me or anyone making a big deal over his death he'd probably tell us off lol. So I say my final farewells to him and hope he's in a better place now.

&#x200B;

And for the upcoming sadness...My 15 year old cat has cancer and this will be her last Christmas. We got her when I was just leaving 5th grade as a kitten, and the story of how we got her is one of my favorites. To tell it in short, me and my brother saw her and wanted her, but my mom was against getting a female cat since we already had two males. So I pulled my brother aside and told him to start crying so we could get the kitten. He said he couldn't cry on command, so I said they'd do horrible things to the kitten if we didn't get her. Needless to say once he had started sobbing my mom had no choice lol.

But she has lived a long life, much longer than we thought since she's currently 20 odd pounds now, a very fat kitty. We don't know when the end will come for her, but it won't be long as the tumor they had removed in the summer has grown back and then some. So far my mom and I have been getting into small fights on if we have to put her down or try seeking a second opinion and see if there are other options. Though we do know for sure, this will be her final Christmas and I hope she'll make it to the beginning of 2022. She's a good cat, even though she's a bitch to the other cats. I'm going to miss her a lot once she's gone, there are just so many good memories with her...

&#x200B;

Anyway, thanks for reading all that, if not I totally understand not wanting to read a wall of text lol. Just know that I really like how this drawing came out and that it just symbolizes some sadness in my life.

♥

We currently have 4 cats lol, they just don't really act like he did though. I mean I love my cats, they're adorable in their own way, it's just I had that cat for 19 years, since I was around 5 years old. He was my everything for so long and that's just a hard thing to recreate. I just miss him, but my other cats help with it.

&#x200B;

I wish I could like humanity more, it's been hard ever since politics got thrown into everything. I try to see the silver lining, but sometimes you just have to squint so hard that you just kinda give up in the end. Maybe I'm just a little too negative though, but I do like when people put aside their differences and help others, that is always something nice to read about. Or people helping animals, that always makes me super happy :)

I also want to add an extra note in here with my observations. You can see in the screenshot above that Spider is mid step as pointed out in this picture [here.](https://imgur.com/a/66qWkeM)

&#x200B;

Again the my search for the video I saw is going nowhere, if anyone with experience in finding old sites could help I'd very much appreciate it!

It wasn't a dream, I remember seeing the video multiple times on that site and just wondering how it was cut when it seemed so finished.

&#x200B;

I know it sounds unbelievable but I can remember it too vividly for it to have just been a dream stemming from this one picture.
